<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>India News | Latest India News Today &amp; Real-time News from India, India Breaking News</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india</link><description>India News Today: Get latest India news and breaking news from India on Times of India. TOI brings the top news headlines from India on Politics, Elections, Current Affairs and more</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-11-10T14:48:36+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/-2128936835.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:48:36 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>India News | Latest India News Today &amp; Real-time News from India, India Breaking News</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india</link></image><item><title><![CDATA['No real contact with him': Sonia Gandhi recalls face-to-face meetings with PM Modi in memoir]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/no-real-contact-with-him-sonia-gandhi-recalls-face-to-face-meetings-with-pm-modi-in-memoir/articleshow/135704446.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135704446.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Sonia Gandhi reveals in her memoir that she has had minimal contact with PM Narendra Modi. Their encounters are restricted to formal greetings at political gatherings, often avoiding eye contact. Gandhi contrasts her vision of an inclusive India with Modi's more exclusionary ideology shaped by the RSS. She also revisits the violence of the 2002 Gujarat riots during Modi's tenure as chief minister.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/no-real-contact-with-him-sonia-gandhi-recalls-face-to-face-meetings-with-pm-modi-in-memoir/articleshow/135704446.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/no-real-contact-with-him-sonia-gandhi-recalls-face-to-face-meetings-with-pm-modi-in-memoir/articleshow/135704446.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-10T14:13:42+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vijaya Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135704547,imgsize-92636.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Should've called it Whitewashing, not Belonging': BJP mocks Sonia Gandhi's memoir]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/shouldve-called-it-whitewashing-not-belonging-bjp-mocks-sonia-gandhis-memoir/articleshow/135701040.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135701040.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[BJP spokesperson CR Kesavan criticized Sonia Gandhi's memoir, arguing it attempts to whitewash the historical mistakes of the Congress party. He highlighted her emotional responses to key incidents while questioning her silence on the 1984 anti-Sikh riots and other tragedies. The memoir details Sonia's childhood, her marriage to Rajiv Gandhi, and her experiences as part of the Gandhi family.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/shouldve-called-it-whitewashing-not-belonging-bjp-mocks-sonia-gandhis-memoir/articleshow/135701040.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/shouldve-called-it-whitewashing-not-belonging-bjp-mocks-sonia-gandhis-memoir/articleshow/135701040.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-10T14:03:30+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Trisha Mahajan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135704904,imgsize-84578.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Managing hashtags and state are different': BJP takes swipe at Vijay over alleged fund theft in Tamil Nadu]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/managing-hashtags-and-state-are-different-bjp-takes-swipe-at-vijay-over-alleged-fund-theft-in-tamil-nadu/articleshow/135702526.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135702526.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/managing-hashtags-and-state-are-different-bjp-takes-swipe-at-vijay-over-alleged-fund-theft-in-tamil-nadu/articleshow/135702526.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/managing-hashtags-and-state-are-different-bjp-takes-swipe-at-vijay-over-alleged-fund-theft-in-tamil-nadu/articleshow/135702526.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-10T13:05:37+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Abhishek Mishra</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135702715,imgsize-663465.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[DIAL rains for relief: Choked Delhi to see another cloud seeding attempt]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/dial-rains-for-relief-choked-delhi-to-see-another-cloud-seeding-attempt/articleshow/135703310.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135703310.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[India’s capital, New Delhi, will attempt cloud seeding to induce rain and address severe pollution. The initiative involves Delhi International Airport Ltd, the Delhi government, and IIT Kanpur. A specialized aircraft from Kyathi Climate will undertake the operation on Tuesday and Wednesday. A fresh western disturbance is expected to bring rain to northwestern India later this week. Cloud seeding aims to enhance precipitation as the air quality deteriorates.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/dial-rains-for-relief-choked-delhi-to-see-another-cloud-seeding-attempt/articleshow/135703310.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/dial-rains-for-relief-choked-delhi-to-see-another-cloud-seeding-attempt/articleshow/135703310.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-10T13:03:40+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Saurabh Sinha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135703495,imgsize-706965.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Warrants urgent attention': SC flags vehicular pollution in Delhi-NCR, seeks action plan]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/warrants-urgent-attention-sc-flags-vehicular-pollution-in-delhi-ncr-seeks-action-plan/articleshow/135702298.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135702298.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The Supreme Court has mandated that Delhi and three adjacent states intensify measures to combat vehicle emissions. Officials are tasked with reporting on the implementation of laws governing aging and non-compliant vehicles. With rising pollution levels in the National Capital Region, the court emphasized the need for inter-state collaboration on vehicle management and stricter adherence to emission standards. The matter will be reviewed again on November 23.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/warrants-urgent-attention-sc-flags-vehicular-pollution-in-delhi-ncr-seeks-action-plan/articleshow/135702298.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/warrants-urgent-attention-sc-flags-vehicular-pollution-in-delhi-ncr-seeks-action-plan/articleshow/135702298.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-10T12:46:22+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Trisha Mahajan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135703007,imgsize-51940.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['I'd quake in my seat': Sonia Gandhi recalls Indira Gandhi's temper, early days as bride in memoir]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/id-quake-in-my-seat-sonia-gandhi-recalls-indira-gandhis-temper-early-days-as-bride-in-memoir/articleshow/135701951.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135701951.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Sonia Gandhi’s memoir, Belonging: A Journey of Love, offers an intimate account of Indira Gandhi’s temper, recalling how staff were made to stand in corners, a senior Congress leader ordered to face a wall and others ignored for days. Sonia also describes Rajiv’s reassurance during her mother-in-law’s outbursts, Indira’s domestic routines, love for sarees and photographs, and how grandchildren gradually softened her temperament.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/id-quake-in-my-seat-sonia-gandhi-recalls-indira-gandhis-temper-early-days-as-bride-in-memoir/articleshow/135701951.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/id-quake-in-my-seat-sonia-gandhi-recalls-indira-gandhis-temper-early-days-as-bride-in-memoir/articleshow/135701951.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-10T12:08:46+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Abhishek Mishra</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135701979,imgsize-568103.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[What made Sonia Gandhi turn down PM post after UPA’s 2004 victory? Memoir revisits moment]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/what-made-sonia-gandhi-turn-down-pm-post-after-upas-2004-victory-memoir-revisits-moment/articleshow/135699936.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135699936.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Sonia Gandhi reveals her thoughts in her memoir about declining the prime minister role after the UPA's victory. She describes her inner voice guiding her decision and her conversation with Rahul. Gandhi highlights why she chose Manmohan Singh for the position, noting his integrity and governance experience. Her memoir also covers her personal journey, including significant tragedies and cultural adjustments after moving to India.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/what-made-sonia-gandhi-turn-down-pm-post-after-upas-2004-victory-memoir-revisits-moment/articleshow/135699936.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/what-made-sonia-gandhi-turn-down-pm-post-after-upas-2004-victory-memoir-revisits-moment/articleshow/135699936.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-10T10:30:14+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vijaya Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135699972,imgsize-912528.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[India, US plan joint crackdown on transnational drug cartels, synthetic drug trade]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/india-us-plan-joint-crackdown-on-transnational-drug-cartels-synthetic-drug-trade/articleshow/135698752.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135698752.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Top security officials from India and the US gathered in New Delhi to address narcotics syndicates. The discussions focused on establishing a framework to combat synthetic drug flows and secure supply chains. NCB Director General Anurag Garg emphasized a network-centric enforcement model to target cartels and facilitators. Both nations endorsed operational milestones, including initiatives to prevent the diversion of synthetic drug precursors.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/india-us-plan-joint-crackdown-on-transnational-drug-cartels-synthetic-drug-trade/articleshow/135698752.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/india-us-plan-joint-crackdown-on-transnational-drug-cartels-synthetic-drug-trade/articleshow/135698752.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-10T09:34:23+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Trisha Mahajan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135698816,imgsize-142716.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Three workers killed during water tank maintenance at Tata iPhone parts factory in Tamil Nadu]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/three-workers-killed-during-water-tank-maintenance-at-tata-iphone-parts-factory-in-tamil-nadu/articleshow/135698027.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135698027.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/three-workers-killed-during-water-tank-maintenance-at-tata-iphone-parts-factory-in-tamil-nadu/articleshow/135698027.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/three-workers-killed-during-water-tank-maintenance-at-tata-iphone-parts-factory-in-tamil-nadu/articleshow/135698027.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-10T09:04:49+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pranjal Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135698166,imgsize-138042.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Hasina seeks passport, Dhaka calls it political stunt &amp; seeks extradition]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/hasina-seeks-passport-dhaka-calls-it-political-stunt-seeks-extradition/articleshow/135697754.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135697754.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Ousted Bangladeshi Prime Minister Sheikh Hasina has requested a new passport from the Bangladesh High Commission. The request aims to facilitate her planned return to Bangladesh after two years in exile. Bangladesh authorities have labeled the request a political stunt and emphasized her extradition due to criminal convictions. Indian officials have stated that the extradition matter should be handled through existing legal processes.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/hasina-seeks-passport-dhaka-calls-it-political-stunt-seeks-extradition/articleshow/135697754.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/hasina-seeks-passport-dhaka-calls-it-political-stunt-seeks-extradition/articleshow/135697754.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-10T08:53:36+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Ahsan Tasnim and Sachin Parashar</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135697905,imgsize-108992.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Global capital for Sanatan pilgrimage': Akhilesh's big Ayodhya promise ahead of 2027 UP polls]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/global-capital-for-sanatan-pilgrimage-akhileshs-big-ayodhya-promise-ahead-of-2027-up-polls/articleshow/135697445.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135697445.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Akhilesh Yadav has articulated a bold vision to elevate Ayodhya as the ultimate hub for Sanatan pilgrimage on a global scale. He stressed the importance of honest temple management and top-notch infrastructure to rejuvenate devotees' trust. Additionally, Yadav has committed to tackling local economic challenges and safeguarding the interests of traditional boatmen.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/global-capital-for-sanatan-pilgrimage-akhileshs-big-ayodhya-promise-ahead-of-2027-up-polls/articleshow/135697445.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/global-capital-for-sanatan-pilgrimage-akhileshs-big-ayodhya-promise-ahead-of-2027-up-polls/articleshow/135697445.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-10T08:41:14+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Trisha Mahajan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135697675,imgsize-64560.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Ahead of peace talks, Zelenskyy seeks PM Modi's help on ceasefire]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ahead-of-peace-talks-zelenskyy-seeks-pm-modis-help-on-ceasefire/articleshow/135695245.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135695245.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Asks For More Steps On Food, Energy Security]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ahead-of-peace-talks-zelenskyy-seeks-pm-modis-help-on-ceasefire/articleshow/135695245.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ahead-of-peace-talks-zelenskyy-seeks-pm-modis-help-on-ceasefire/articleshow/135695245.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-10T04:13:58+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Sachin Parashar</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135695277,imgsize-1321379.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Fearing winter polls, Ladakh politi